<title>UK: BOE FORECASTS SURPLUS, DOES NOT OPERATE. [CORRECTED 13:02 GMT]</title>
<headline>BOE FORECASTS SURPLUS, DOES NOT OPERATE. [CORRECTED 13:02 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England did not offer the UK money market assistance in the midday round after forecasting a 250 million stg liquidity surplus in the market.</p>
<p>The Bank had earlier forecast a liquidity shortage of 150 million stg. (Corrects to make clear the Bank of England did not operate in the money market).</p>
</text>
